  "version": 1,
  "description": "The machine-readable list of setup features a GAIA project or machine can decide on. The setup command records one decision per listed id (applied, declined, or not-applicable) in the project config for project-scope ids and in the per-machine setup state for machine-scope ids, and the update flow reads the list against those records to find features a project has not yet decided. Each entry names its scope, whether the setup phase applies it without asking (required), whether applying it needs a repository admin (admin), whether its reference can run on its own with only what it probes itself (standalone), and the reference file that owns the feature. Ids are stable: a feature that changes meaning gets a new id and the old one retires. Every id added after the first set must be standalone.",
